    complete under the default bounds; the three vector formats link `:ok`
    retaining exactly `#{+ *}`; the tree format: see finding 4.1. No
    wall-clock assertion.
- [`test/yin/vm/linker_manifest_test.cljc`](../test/yin/vm/linker_manifest_test.cljc):
  - `a-verifying-derivation-fetches-the-tree-without-scanning-it`: a
    `counting-ast-format` record (validator and three scanners wrapped) in
    the test's own format map; per vector format the `:verifying` link is
    `:ok`, `:trust :verified`, the tree validator ran, and the three scanner
    counts sum to 0; a requested `:yin.ast/code` link still runs each scanner
    once (L1);
  - `publish-and-link-local-take-caller-bounds`: an 8-row module under
    `{:bounds {:max-parts 4}}` is refused
    `:yin.link.publish/incomplete-closure` with `:parts-limit` in the walk;
    under the default it publishes with every format `:ok`; `link-local`
    under `{:bounds {:max-parts 4}}` is `:parts-limit :max-parts` and `:ok`
    without.
- [`test/yin/vm/linker_require_test.cljc`](../test/yin/vm/linker_require_test.cljc):
  `a-serving-composition-names-the-trust-it-applied`: a real
  `yin.repl.link` composition over a published store answers one by-name
  request per lowered format: default `:trust :verified`,
  `{:derivation :trusted}` `:trust :composition`.

Red phase (before steps 2 to 6): 16 failures and 1 error on the JVM, every one
